                <pb facs="0941" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg825"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate, Ciudad
                            Juárez</hi></placeName>,<lb/>[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-08-20">undated</date>] (<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            August 20, 1912—11.45 p.m.</hi>)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Federals occupied Juárez to-day. Civil government to be established to-morrow and
                    railroad traffic resumed. General belief that revolution is ended in State of
                    Chihuahua; refugees will now return to their homes. General rejoicing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
